course: dictionary
lesson: 4169
title: Gobble: eating, turkeys and taking over
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: One word can have more than one meaning. «Gobble» can mean eating very fast, the sound a turkey makes, or using something up quickly. Context tells you which one: «Po gobbles dumplings» is about food, but «Only male turkeys gobble» is about a sound.
explain: Look at the words near gobble. If someone is eating with a full mouth and no pause, gobble means eat fast. If the subject is a turkey, it means the throaty gobble-gobble sound. Swap your meaning into the sentence to check it still makes sense.
explain: The phrases gobble up and gobble down help too. «Fees gobble up savings» means the fees use up the money quickly, not that anyone is eating it.
fact: To gobble means to eat something very quickly and greedily.
fact: «Gobble» can also mean the throaty sound a male turkey makes, and it is a noun too: a gobble.
fact: To gobble up means to use up or take over something quickly, like savings or land.
fact: «Only male turkeys gobble», to attract females and warn rivals.
fact: In Kung Fu Panda, Po gobbles dumplings, but real giant pandas live on bamboo.
exercise: «Po gobbles his dumplings in one big bite.» What does gobbles mean? | To paint a picture | To sleep in a warm bed | *To eat very quickly and greedily | To sing a happy song
exercise: «Only male turkeys gobble.» What is a gobble in this sentence? | *The throaty sound a turkey makes | A kind of bread | A big farm building | A tiny bird that can fly fast
exercise: «Fees gobble up the savings.» What does gobble up mean here? | *To use up quickly | To give away for free | To count carefully | To hide under a bed
test: «Cartoon ducks gobble whole loaves of bread.» Which word is closest in meaning to gobble? | Measure | *Devour | Admire
test: «Farm turkeys are bred so heavy that they can hardly fly.» What does hardly mean here? | Very easily | Very loudly | *Only just
exam: Which sentence uses gobble as the turkey sound? | *The turkey began to gobble at dawn | Fees gobble up the savings | The wolf gobbled Grandma | Ella will gobble her lunch in a minute
